{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"panicky-sylphish-foxterrier","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Add an mcp autodeploy target to infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh + the timer, per the ADR 0079 amendment: MCP build-context/path change detection, an MCP /health in-flight-equivalent drain signal so a redeploy never kills an in-flight MCP op (esp. certified plan/code/completion ops), preserving the never-touch-gerrit + bounded-blast-radius + rollback guarantees. Independently verifiable: a source change to MCP triggers only an mcp rebuild; the drain gate blocks redeploy while in_flight>0.","id":"6964-40bb-46c9-48a7","parent_id":"jira-reb-3527","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Extend autodeploy (ADR 0079) to an mcp target with its own in-flight drain gate"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787594463836524001,"uuid":"94629716-e8c0-40ff-80e0-c95846f0049d"}